# weak_dead.tkr — the COL-F0d `weak_get` fixture (crumb 0024). `main.tks` wraps one region
# (`retain`), then drops the last strong reference (`release`, count 1→0, freeing it) — proving
# `weak_get` on the now-freed target returns `null` (does not keep it alive, does not read freed
# memory). The compiler holds no `weak_get` callers, so this path is not fixpoint-exercised.
# Pinned to the C backend: `weak_get` emits on the C route only.

Feature: weak_dead — weak_get on a freed target returns null

  Scenario: a_weak_read_after_the_last_release_returns_null
    Given env = ["TEKO_BACKEND=c"]
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 0
